error[E1001]: `xs[1].len` is used here after its value moved away
 --> mem:///main.lu:7:14
  |
5 |     let ys = move xs
  |                   -- `xs[1]` moved here
6 |     xs[0] = [5]
7 |     ys.len + xs[1].len
  |              ^^^^^^^^^ used after the move
  |
  = note: `xs[1].len` is part of `xs[1]`; moving one empties the other. Disjoint fields stay
    usable.
  = note: re-initializing the place (assigning to it) also makes it usable again.
help: to keep the original, copy it at the move
  |
5 |     let ys = move copy xs
  |
